  "preamble": "Allophonic labialization of /h/ to the voiceless bilabial fricative [ɸ] before rounded vowels and /w/. Three neighbouring languages of Northeast Asia from three unrelated families share the rule. In Standard Japanese /h/ is [ɸ] before /u/ (ふ /hu/ [ɸɯ]). In Korean /h/ becomes labialized [ɸʷ] before /o/, /u/ and /w/. In Ainu /h/ is heard as [ɸ] before /u/. The lip rounding of the following vowel or glide is anticipated during the glottal friction, so the fricative moves to the lips.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Labialization, Coarticulation",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Japanese",
      "languageFamily": "Japonic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "/hune/",
          "to": "[ɸɯ̟ne̞] fune 'boat'",
          "note": "/h/ is realized as [ɸ] before /u/; it is [h] before /a, e, o/ and [ç] before /i/"
        },
        {
          "from": "/huju/",
          "to": "[ɸɯ̟jɯ̟] fuyu 'winter'",
          "note": "Same allophone before /u/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Korean",
      "languageFamily": "Koreanic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "후추 /hutɕʰu/",
          "to": "[ɸʷut͡ɕʰu] 'black pepper'",
          "note": "/h/ becomes bilabial [ɸʷ] before /u/"
        },
        {
          "from": "호수 /hosu/",
          "to": "[ɸʷo̞sʰu] 'lake'",
          "note": "Before /o/"
        },
        {
          "from": "화 /hwa/",
          "to": "[ɸwa̠] 'anger'",
          "note": "Before the labial glide /w/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Ainu",
      "languageFamily": "Ainu",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "hu フ /hu/",
          "to": "[ɸu̜]",
          "note": "/h/ is heard as [ɸ] before /u/; ha, he, ho keep [h] and hi is [çi]"
        },
        {
          "from": "huy フィ /hui/",
          "to": "[ɸu̜ɪ]",
          "note": "Same allophone before /u/ in the diphthong"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
